  "step1DetailTitle": "Who Can Vote?",
  "step1DetailBody": "To be eligible to vote in Indian elections, you must be:\n\n• A citizen of India\n• At least 18 years of age on the qualifying date\n• An ordinary resident of the constituency\n• Not disqualified by law\n\nQualifying dates: January 1, April 1, July 1, October 1",
  "step2DetailTitle": "How to Register",
  "step2DetailBody": "Register as a new voter through:\n\n1. Online: Visit voters.eci.gov.in and fill Form 6\n2. Voter Helpline App\n3. Offline: Visit your local ERO/BLO office\n\nDocuments needed: Proof of age, address, and passport photo",
  "step3DetailTitle": "Verify Your Voter ID",
  "step3DetailBody": "After registration:\n\n1. Visit electoralsearch.eci.gov.in\n2. Search by name or EPIC number\n3. Check polling station details\n4. Download your e-EPIC",
  "step4DetailTitle": "Key Election Dates",
  "step4DetailBody": "Important milestones:\n\n• Announcement of schedule\n• Nomination filing\n• Scrutiny of nominations\n• Withdrawal deadline\n• Campaigning period (ends 48hrs before polling)\n• Polling Day\n• Counting Day\n• Results Declaration",
  "step5DetailTitle": "Voting Day Guide",
  "step5DetailBody": "On voting day:\n\n1. Locate your booth via Voter Helpline App\n2. Carry your Voter ID or approved photo ID\n3. Get verified and ink-marked\n4. Press button next to your candidate on EVM\n5. Verify on VVPAT slip\n6. Exit the booth\n\nPolling hours: typically 7 AM to 6 PM",
  "step6DetailTitle": "How Results are Declared",
  "step6DetailBody": "After polling:\n\n1. EVMs sealed and stored securely\n2. Counting day: usually 3-4 days after last phase\n3. EVM votes counted, matched with VVPAT samples\n4. Results declared in rounds\n5. Winner receives Certificate of Election\n\nLive results at results.eci.gov.in"
